-   $$ \frac{dp}{d\_mean} = p \cdot \Sigma^{-1} \Delta $$
-   For the Conic variant, $\Sigma^{-1}$ is replaced by the conic matrix $C$.
-   $$ \frac{dp}{d\_mean} = p \cdot C \Delta $$
-
-6. **Compute Gradient w.r.t. Covariance/Conic ($d_p/d\_cov$):**
